WEBVTT

00:02.170 --> 00:04.790
"Determine": to decide on blah, blah, blah.

00:05.290 --> 00:08.250
"Establish": to set up blah, blah, blah.

00:08.960 --> 00:11.630
"Maintain": to preserve blah, blah, blah.

00:12.630 --> 00:17.170
I have practically zero time for this,
and exams are coming up.

00:17.330 --> 00:21.040
Are those your vocab cards?
I thought they were the Heart Sutra.

00:21.040 --> 00:22.670
I practice Shinto!

00:24.500 --> 00:29.080
But I am in big trouble.
I've only been hanging out recently.

00:29.790 --> 00:35.540
Yolde-sama and Hima-chan came by,
and the spirits went astray, and I bought a mature coat...

00:32.040 --> 00:33.250
<b>What's up, suckers?</b>

00:35.710 --> 00:37.130
That's pretty normal, right?

00:37.130 --> 00:40.880
And you can generally get
what's on the test if you listen in class.

00:41.250 --> 00:43.380
That's because you're a genius type, Koma-chan!

00:43.460 --> 00:46.380
You were always playing around
next to me while I studied!

00:47.130 --> 00:49.210
Normal people have to grind away studying for tests!

00:50.000 --> 00:51.830
"Suffer: to be in pain."

00:52.250 --> 00:54.710
"Struggle: to writhe in agony."

00:55.250 --> 00:58.790
I think you're always doing your best, though. Seriously!

00:59.290 --> 01:02.130
Thanks, buddy, but I'm still annoyed.

02:33.170 --> 02:36.000
<b>TAKAMIMI SHRINE</b>

02:33.170 --> 02:37.830
<b>EPISODE 6</b>

02:41.170 --> 02:44.630
They truly are cool! These Mobile Samurai Gongem...

02:44.880 --> 02:48.960
The normal version is all "Burn up! Burn up!"

02:49.080 --> 02:54.130
And this limited edition clear version
is all "Rise up! Rise from the dead!"

02:55.500 --> 02:57.330
Oh, it's already time!

02:58.000 --> 03:00.080
Koito is going to be back soon.

03:02.130 --> 03:06.670
Recently, Koito hasn't been coming here often
unless it's for rituals.

03:07.250 --> 03:09.330
Sorry, I'm a little busy today.

03:10.790 --> 03:14.000
Could she have finally gotten sick and tired of me?!

03:14.000 --> 03:18.250
I... mean... I mean... I can come up
with a lot of reasons why!

03:18.460 --> 03:20.420
Don't fall asleep in the middle of the rituals!

03:20.830 --> 03:22.880
You know you only get one Red Bull a day!

03:23.250 --> 03:26.040
You bought another new model kit
even though you aren't building any of them?!

03:30.330 --> 03:33.290
All right, today I'm gonna study hard!

03:34.130 --> 03:35.580
W-welcome home, Koito!

03:35.710 --> 03:37.830
Whoa! You scared me!

03:38.000 --> 03:41.500
C-can you stop by for a bit?
We can have tea or something.

03:41.500 --> 03:45.380
Oh, sorry. I'm kinda busy, so I'll be by later.

03:46.880 --> 03:49.210
Eh? O-okay.

03:51.580 --> 03:54.540
I-I knew it. She's sick of me!

04:00.210 --> 04:02.670
Koito dropped something.

04:11.130 --> 04:14.130
<b>ANUHTHER SHRINE</b>

04:11.130 --> 04:14.130
<b>ACADEMIC ACHIEVEMENT</b>

04:11.130 --> 04:14.130
<b>ANUHTHER SHRINE</b>

04:15.460 --> 04:16.580
She's unfaithful!

04:20.960 --> 04:22.920
You promiscuous miko!

04:22.920 --> 04:23.750
Huh?!

04:25.250 --> 04:27.250
Oh! My amulet!

04:27.710 --> 04:31.580
Explain! Why do you have amulets
from Anuhther Shrine?!

04:31.750 --> 04:37.750
U-um, well, er... We don't offer
any amulets for schoolwork here, so...

04:38.330 --> 04:42.290
Koito, there's still time before entrance exams.
Why would you need an amulet for school?

04:42.630 --> 04:46.500
I have a test coming up soon.
I don't have much confidence in myself this time.

04:47.000 --> 04:50.500
W-well then... that's what this is about?

04:52.710 --> 04:56.380
I was certain that you had gotten sick of me, Koito.

04:57.330 --> 04:59.130
I would never!

04:59.500 --> 05:02.210
Great! Now let's hang out, Koito!

05:02.460 --> 05:04.290
Were you even listening?

05:10.790 --> 05:15.040
<b>Math</b>

05:12.170 --> 05:14.880
Studying is rough, no matter the era.

05:15.630 --> 05:19.500
Speaking of, how did you learn this language, Elda?

05:19.830 --> 05:22.710
Was it the uh... those temple schools?

05:23.630 --> 05:26.790
When I was summoned here,
there was still no such thing as a temple school,

05:27.040 --> 05:30.460
so at the beginning, I learned words by listening.

05:35.080 --> 05:37.330
They are probably angry...

05:38.130 --> 05:42.250
So, when the temple school system started,
I learned to read and write there.

05:43.630 --> 05:44.670
Was it hard?

05:45.000 --> 05:48.500
Yes. I got my ears pulled on
by the children and things like that.

05:48.830 --> 05:50.540
Th-that's unfortunate.

05:51.170 --> 05:54.750
But I still appreciated the chance to learn properly.

05:55.210 --> 05:57.630
Oh, I didn't know you struggled with this, too.

05:58.170 --> 06:03.960
By the way, in Edo alone there were around
1,300 temple schools including small and large ones.

06:04.250 --> 06:08.210
That's why a fair amount of people
in the Edo area could read and write.

06:08.460 --> 06:12.710
The literacy rate of Japan at the time
was one of the best in the entire world.

06:15.710 --> 06:17.670
Oh crud! I got caught up in our conversation!

06:17.880 --> 06:21.960
I-I have to study! Sorry, I'll see you later, Elda!

06:21.960 --> 06:23.630
Oh, th-that's fine.

06:28.420 --> 06:29.250
Glance.

06:39.710 --> 06:41.380
K-Koito...?

06:41.580 --> 06:42.920
Whoa! You're still here?!

06:43.380 --> 06:46.420
A-actually, there's something I couldn't say earlier...

06:46.540 --> 06:48.500
It's about the temple school.

06:48.750 --> 06:50.630
S-something you forgot to say?

06:51.170 --> 06:54.540
The truth is, the temple schools were only called that
in the Kyoto-Osaka area.

06:55.080 --> 06:58.630
In Edo they didn't like to add the "ya" part
that refers to it as a sort of room,

06:57.040 --> 06:57.750
<b>Ya (Room)</b>

06:58.630 --> 07:01.580
so they used names like
"Brush Learning Center" and ”Penmanship."

06:58.750 --> 06:59.500
<b>Brush Learning Center</b>

06:59.750 --> 07:00.540
<b>Penmanship</b>

07:02.330 --> 07:04.500
Right. A-and what about it?

07:06.790 --> 07:07.630
That's it.

07:07.710 --> 07:09.080
What? That's all?!

07:09.080 --> 07:10.330
Y-yeah.

07:10.580 --> 07:14.460
O-oh, okay. "Penmanship," huh? Got it.

07:20.880 --> 07:23.380
I-it's a little warm today.

07:23.380 --> 07:24.460
Sure is.

07:24.710 --> 07:28.330
O-on days like this,
I start craving chocolate mint ice cream.

07:28.790 --> 07:30.330
Yeah... Mm-hmm.

07:30.960 --> 07:35.920
Oh, right! When I was organizing the bookshelves
I found some books that I think you might like.

07:36.750 --> 07:39.290
Here! A fashion magazine from 20 years ago!

07:39.500 --> 07:40.830
I wasn't even born yet!

07:44.960 --> 07:47.500
But there's still some cute stuff.

07:47.880 --> 07:50.540
Th-they say trends will repeat themselves.

07:52.420 --> 07:55.080
No, stop this! I've got to study!

07:55.250 --> 07:57.830
Just hang out with me, Koito!

07:57.830 --> 07:58.830
How old are you?!

08:02.500 --> 08:08.580
You know, I don't want people to think that my job
as a miko is interfering with my studies.

08:09.000 --> 08:14.130
A major ritual is coming up soon, so I want to make sure
I do my best when I'm studying for the test.

08:15.460 --> 08:17.290
S-so that's what's going on.

08:17.710 --> 08:19.250
Do you understand?

08:19.250 --> 08:19.920
Yup!

08:20.630 --> 08:25.040
Basically, you have to work hard right now
because you want to hang out with me more later!

08:25.290 --> 08:29.040
Hmm, I feel like you're kind of missing the point,
but yeah, we'll go with that.

08:29.920 --> 08:34.000
O-okay! I'll help you out, too, so good luck, Koito!

08:34.130 --> 08:36.420
You're helping? Are you going to do something for me?

08:36.540 --> 08:39.170
I'll keep quiet in the main temple,
and spend some time alone!

08:39.170 --> 08:40.290
You're a life saver!

08:48.000 --> 08:49.960
<b>Japanese Dictionary</b>

08:53.130 --> 08:54.580
Dang it...

08:55.420 --> 09:01.380
<b>Detailed</b>

08:55.420 --> 09:01.380
<b>Japanese History B</b>

08:55.920 --> 08:58.830
I-it's gotten pretty messy in here.

08:59.040 --> 09:00.790
I guess I'll tidy up a little.

09:11.920 --> 09:14.040
A-an hour's already passed!

09:15.630 --> 09:18.460
Oh no, this is bad! Gotta study, gotta study!

09:23.790 --> 09:25.880
Oh, a text from Hima-chan.

09:28.380 --> 09:30.000
Yolde-sama's adorable!

09:31.420 --> 09:34.580
While I've already got my smartphone,
may as well check Insta really quick.

09:35.960 --> 09:41.170
Her pictures always look amazing.
That's Isuzu Koimari-chan, huh...?

09:44.580 --> 09:47.080
I-I lost another hour?!

09:48.500 --> 09:52.880
I have to focus! Time is just slipping away...

09:53.830 --> 09:58.210
It's times like this
that I wish I had someone to study with me.

09:59.710 --> 10:02.170
<b>Detailed</b>

09:59.710 --> 10:02.170
<b>Japanese History B</b>

09:59.710 --> 10:02.170
<b>A textbook to take notes in</b>

09:59.710 --> 10:02.170
<b>Revised Ed.</b>

10:00.670 --> 10:01.460
I know!

10:08.040 --> 10:10.290
I hope Koito is working hard.

10:11.460 --> 10:12.290
Elda!

10:13.880 --> 10:18.500
Y-you scared me, Koito! Are you done studying?

10:18.500 --> 10:23.250
Nope! But actually, I was thinking when I have questions
about the history of Japan, I could ask you!

10:23.880 --> 10:26.830
You're the Takamimi Hime-no-Mikoto
who saw this history with her own two eyes!

10:27.080 --> 10:30.040
There's no doubt I'll get a high score
in Japanese history now!

10:30.170 --> 10:36.880
I-I see, it's true that if it's about Japanese history,
I may know a bit about it.

10:37.000 --> 10:39.630
Right?! Here's a question to try it out!

10:40.880 --> 10:42.210
Let's see...

10:42.540 --> 10:44.500
In the Edo shogunate's feudal lord division,

10:44.500 --> 10:49.250
what were the feudal lords who followed
the Tokugawa Clan after the Battle of Sekigahara called?

10:49.500 --> 10:50.710
"Tozama Feudal Lords."

10:51.000 --> 10:52.580
Wow! That was spot on!

10:54.420 --> 10:55.130
What's wrong?

10:55.920 --> 10:57.920
I had a hard time back then.

10:58.290 --> 11:04.420
Ever since I was summoned by Ieyasu-kun,
I never got along well with those Tozama people.

11:04.580 --> 11:06.540
It was extremely awkward.

11:06.880 --> 11:09.790
O-oh, that sounds rough.

11:10.460 --> 11:13.540
N-now, pull yourself together,
and on to the next question!

11:14.210 --> 11:18.630
What was the name of the Dutch ship
that drifted ashore in Bungo in 1600?

11:19.540 --> 11:20.580
Liefde.

11:21.040 --> 11:23.250
Correct! Nice going, Elda!

11:26.210 --> 11:28.460
I had a hard time back then.

11:28.790 --> 11:34.790
The diplomatic trade advisors Jan-kun and William-kun
would always call out to me in a foreign language...

11:35.170 --> 11:38.210
I had no idea what they were saying,
and it was extremely awkward.

11:39.420 --> 11:45.290
What was the event in 1867 where the masses
danced enthusiastically in groups called?

11:45.750 --> 11:47.080
"Ee ja nai ka."

11:47.750 --> 11:49.830
I had a hard time back then.

11:50.080 --> 11:53.290
I'm awful at flash mobs, so it was extremely awk-

11:53.290 --> 11:56.630
Your history of Japan is full of awkward stories!

11:56.630 --> 12:00.290
I mean, you have so many worthless stories,
I have no idea what to expect!

12:02.130 --> 12:04.750
I have no choice but to do some honest hard work!

12:05.040 --> 12:06.290
Thanks for having me.

12:06.920 --> 12:08.540
G-good luck, Koito.

12:09.210 --> 12:10.080
Yeah...

12:11.080 --> 12:14.170
Oh no, she's completely lost motivation.

12:14.750 --> 12:18.420
Koito is my miko. I have to encourage her!

12:19.040 --> 12:21.920
Is there... maybe something I can say?

12:22.790 --> 12:27.500
I-I've got it! If you get a good score,
I'll treat you to some delicious sushi!

12:31.080 --> 12:32.000
Koito?

12:36.080 --> 12:37.580
REALLY?

12:39.210 --> 12:44.210
Oh. My spending money... that'll clear me out.

12:44.630 --> 12:49.580
<b>Sushi</b>

12:44.630 --> 12:49.580
<b>Sushi</b>

12:44.630 --> 12:49.580
<b>Sushi</b>

12:44.710 --> 12:54.420
Sushi, sushi, sushi, sushi, sushi...

12:56.670 --> 13:02.750
Oh, please... I pray that Koito bombs this test.

13:04.540 --> 13:12.420
Elda's sorrowful plea vanished like a bubble,
and Koito got a very good score.

13:21.250 --> 13:23.830
Tsukishima, Chuo City, Tokyo.

13:24.880 --> 13:29.420
Spanning more than 400 years
since the Edo Period, is Takamimi Shrine.

13:26.880 --> 13:29.830
<b>TAKAMIMI SHRINE</b>

13:30.330 --> 13:37.380
The goddess summoned from another world
enshrined here was an absolute social recluse of an elf.

13:38.290 --> 13:41.920
They said it'd be about two hours after sunrise.
The skies will be clear.

13:42.540 --> 13:44.630
I hope we get a good view of Mt. Fuji.

13:45.710 --> 13:46.290
Yeah.

13:46.500 --> 13:47.710
Speak up!

13:48.130 --> 13:49.710
A-are you okay, Elda?

13:50.330 --> 13:53.670
I've been so anxious and tense
I haven't slept for two or three days...

13:54.040 --> 13:58.000
Today is the Shinto ritual that happens
once every 50 years! Snap out of it, come on!

13:59.080 --> 14:01.920
I've never liked high places...

14:02.290 --> 14:05.080
But, why did I have to be the driver?

14:05.420 --> 14:07.880
You could've at least gone to the Skytree by taxi, right?

14:08.040 --> 14:13.040
M-my heart can't take being in such a small place
with people I don't know.

14:13.170 --> 14:16.040
Strengthen your heart! You're a 621-year-old child!

14:18.460 --> 14:20.790
Today is a major ritual that happens once every 50 years.

14:21.420 --> 14:27.580
We stand at the highest point in Tokyo and face Mt. Fuji,
and pray for Lord Ieyasu Tokugawa to protect Edo.

14:28.130 --> 14:29.540
It's a ritual of worshipping Mt Fuji from afar.

14:31.250 --> 14:35.170
I-it's scary out there!
And places high up are even scarier!

14:35.170 --> 14:36.880
My gosh, shut up!

14:40.040 --> 14:41.330
Well, good luck up there.

14:41.630 --> 14:43.630
Right! Thanks, Akane-chan!

14:44.000 --> 14:46.250
T-take me back with you!

14:46.790 --> 14:49.040
My mom will be here to take you home.

14:49.880 --> 14:53.130
A-Akane!

14:53.290 --> 14:57.290
<b>Welcome</b>

14:53.290 --> 14:57.290
<b>Takamimi Hime-no-Mikoto-sama</b>

14:53.290 --> 14:57.290
<b>Route</b>

14:53.790 --> 14:54.920
Looks like it's this way!

14:55.080 --> 14:57.210
I wonder if the staff posted it up for us.

14:57.460 --> 14:58.500
Let's go, Elda!

15:00.540 --> 15:05.420
Yay! This is my first time
going up the Skytree! I can't wait!

15:06.130 --> 15:08.830
Is this place... a shopping center?

15:08.830 --> 15:12.250
It's a shopping center, but it's called Tokyo Skytree Town.

15:12.830 --> 15:15.040
There are lots of trendy shops here.

15:16.040 --> 15:18.920
I've come here with Koma-chan before.

15:19.130 --> 15:24.330
Yet you didn't go up there?
What's with that? You're scared too, huh, Koito?

15:24.500 --> 15:29.580
No way. I couldn't go up to the observation gallery
because I was short on funds.

15:30.040 --> 15:32.750
We couldn't do anything about it,
so we ate five crepes and went home.

15:33.170 --> 15:36.040
You should've used the crepe money to go up there.

15:36.040 --> 15:37.960
Promise not to mention that.

15:38.750 --> 15:42.210
But you know, I'm glad we're able
to use the Skytree for this.

15:42.790 --> 15:46.960
I-I heard from the staff that there are people
from Tsukishima here.

15:46.960 --> 15:51.500
Kikujiro asked for the heck of it,
and they gladly gave the OK.

15:51.500 --> 15:53.750
Wow, good going, gramps.

15:54.040 --> 15:56.670
It wasn't necessary for Kikujiro to do that...

15:56.830 --> 15:58.330
What are you talking about?

15:58.330 --> 15:59.670
I-I mean...

16:00.210 --> 16:04.210
In the Edo days, even though we could see
Mt. Fuji from the Nihombashi bridge,

16:04.210 --> 16:06.670
it's all nothing but tall buildings now.

16:07.130 --> 16:10.790
Wow, so you did this ceremony in Nihombashi too?

16:11.250 --> 16:16.210
No. Since the tallest building was Edo Castle,
we held it there.

16:11.630 --> 16:14.290
<b>Mobile Samurai Gongem</b>

16:11.630 --> 16:14.290
<b>18 meters</b>

16:16.580 --> 16:19.580
It was 60 meters high and so scary...

16:17.210 --> 16:19.210
<b>Edo Castle</b>

16:17.210 --> 16:19.210
<b>60 meters</b>

16:20.000 --> 16:25.130
In the Meiji times, it was in the Ryounkaku building
in Asakusa, and it was a little lower so that was a relief...

16:20.920 --> 16:23.380
<b>Ryounkaku</b>

16:20.920 --> 16:23.380
<b>52 meters</b>

16:25.420 --> 16:30.920
From then on, the places got higher, and the Skytree
we're using this year is a terrifying 634 meters!

16:29.460 --> 16:31.630
<b>Tokyo Skytree</b>

16:29.460 --> 16:31.630
<b>634 meters</b>

16:31.170 --> 16:35.130
The observation gallery
that we're going to is only at 450 meters!

16:33.000 --> 16:34.790
<b>Observation Gallery</b>

16:33.000 --> 16:34.790
<b>450 meters</b>

16:35.210 --> 16:42.080
It gets higher and higher each time!
Why do humans keep making buildings taller and taller?!

16:42.540 --> 16:45.330
I don't need you to complain to me about humans!

16:48.580 --> 16:52.000
It says we can get to the observation gallery by elevator.

16:56.540 --> 16:58.130
It's so pretty!

16:59.080 --> 17:01.540
<b>Tremble</b>

16:59.080 --> 17:01.540
<b>Tremble</b>

16:59.090 --> 17:01.540
<b>Tremble</b>

17:04.540 --> 17:07.920
Are you okay? You really do hate heights, don't you?

17:08.210 --> 17:13.960
Y-yeah... I've fainted from watching a celebrity
bungee jumping on TV before.

17:14.500 --> 17:16.080
At least you're consistent.

17:16.290 --> 17:18.250
How about thinking of something fun?

17:18.750 --> 17:20.670
I-I'll try it...

17:21.420 --> 17:22.960
The Skytree Town from earlier...

17:23.170 --> 17:23.710
Good.

17:24.290 --> 17:26.170
I wonder if they have a plastic model shop.

17:26.170 --> 17:30.290
Huh? E-er, I wonder... there might be...

17:30.380 --> 17:32.380
They should make a plastic model shop.

17:32.670 --> 17:36.630
Japan's plastic models are world-renowned
for their superb quality.

17:36.630 --> 17:40.880
At tourist spots like Tokyo Skytree Town
that expect an inbound demand,

17:40.880 --> 17:43.000
they should absolutely make a plastic model shop.

17:43.000 --> 17:45.080
The product is not only targeted
at the otaku demographic,

17:45.080 --> 17:49.460
but also has value as a craft
of the new generation of Japan...

17:47.130 --> 17:49.460
Okay! I get it, chill out!

17:52.290 --> 17:58.460
But I wonder, why do we face Mt. Fuji and pray?
Lord Ieyasu was in Edo Castle, right?

17:58.670 --> 18:05.130
No, Ieyasu-kun wasn't in the castle often.
Most of his time was spent in Sunpu Castle.

18:05.630 --> 18:08.130
You can see Mt. Fuji up close from there.

18:06.380 --> 18:07.420
<b>Sunpu Castle</b>

18:08.210 --> 18:10.170
Oh, I didn't know that.

18:10.670 --> 18:15.460
He was also in Suruga when he was younger...
It seems he spent time in present-day Shizuoka,

18:15.750 --> 18:18.540
and he had a very strong attachment to Mt. Fuji.

18:19.250 --> 18:23.130
Maybe the reason he placed the shogunate in Edo
was because he could see Mt. Fuji from there.

18:23.960 --> 18:25.880
I don't know his true motivations, though.

18:26.420 --> 18:31.460
But, when I see Mt. Fuji,
for some reason Ieyasu-kun comes to mind.

18:38.250 --> 18:43.250
The people of Edo loved that mountain, too.
There were Fujizuka all over the place.

18:43.500 --> 18:44.500
Fujizuka?

18:44.920 --> 18:49.080
Small mounds made throughout the town
in the image of Mt. Fuji.

18:49.460 --> 18:53.170
It was an extremely hard task
to go to Mt. Fuji back in the Edo Period,

18:53.290 --> 18:56.210
so Fujizuka were visited and worshipped instead.

18:56.790 --> 19:01.960
Maybe I'll make my own Fujizuka...
then I wouldn't have to go to such tall places.

19:02.250 --> 19:05.170
Wouldn't Lord Ieyasu be angry
about that in the end, too?

19:05.960 --> 19:08.960
Speaking of, why did they choose
the characters meaning "Mountain of Wealth"

19:08.960 --> 19:10.290
when writing Mt. Fuji in kanji?

19:10.290 --> 19:13.040
It doesn't really have the image of growing vegetation.

19:13.330 --> 19:17.630
There's an explanation that Mt. Fuji's name
has origins in Princess Kaguya.

19:17.750 --> 19:20.000
Princess Kaguya? The folk tale?

19:20.500 --> 19:30.330
<b>THE TALE OF</b>

19:20.500 --> 19:30.330
<b>THE BAMBOO CUTTER</b>

19:20.580 --> 19:24.670
The Tale of the Bamboo Cutter
was created in the Heian Period.

19:24.920 --> 19:29.920
The folk tale you know
may be a shortened and edited version.

19:30.460 --> 19:33.250
At the end, Princess Kaguya returns to the moon, right?

19:33.460 --> 19:39.460
When she bid him farewell, she gives her beloved
a secret elixir for eternal youth and immortality.

19:40.290 --> 19:41.540
Eternal youth and immortality...

19:41.830 --> 19:48.580
However, as he was crushed and saddened,
he went to the summit of the highest mountain in Japan,

19:48.790 --> 19:51.460
and burned the secret elixir up.

19:51.920 --> 19:55.000
Then, that mountain became
one of eternal youth and immortality...

19:55.000 --> 19:59.290
A "fu-shi-yama"... and it came to be called "Fujiyama."

20:03.710 --> 20:06.830
Elda sometimes makes this face and smiles.

20:07.960 --> 20:11.040
I don't really like that face.

20:11.880 --> 20:14.080
<b>Welcome</b>

20:11.880 --> 20:14.080
<b>Takamimi Hime-no-Mikoto-sama</b>

20:11.880 --> 20:14.080
<b>You're almost at the highest point</b>

20:13.540 --> 20:16.540
Look, we're almost at the tallest point!

20:16.750 --> 20:17.960
You've got this, Elda!

20:17.960 --> 20:19.460
R-right...

20:19.920 --> 20:22.420
I hope we can see Mt. Fuji clearly.

20:27.580 --> 20:31.500
Hold my hand, Elda!
Then you won't be scared of being so high, right?

20:31.670 --> 20:33.170
No, I'm still scared.

20:33.460 --> 20:35.380
This just means we'll fall together now, you know?

20:35.710 --> 20:37.500
Why are you assuming we'll fall?

20:38.080 --> 20:40.040
Okay then, want to walk alone?

20:41.500 --> 20:44.380
B-but, on second thought, hold my hand please!

20:45.170 --> 20:46.000
Okay!

20:49.790 --> 20:51.670
<b>Welcome</b>

20:49.790 --> 20:51.670
<b>Takamimi Hime-no-Mikoto-sama</b>

20:49.790 --> 20:51.670
<b>The highest point is right ahead of you</b>

20:49.790 --> 20:51.670
<b>Holy sanctuary starts here</b>

20:50.330 --> 20:51.630
We're here!

20:51.960 --> 20:54.750
Right ahead of us is the highest spot in Tokyo!

20:54.960 --> 20:58.380
W-we're way up here! We're basically in the sky!

21:00.330 --> 21:01.830
<b>Holy sanctuary</b>

21:00.880 --> 21:06.080
I see. Ahead of us is the holy sanctuary... I can't go there.

21:07.130 --> 21:10.130
I can't walk to the very end with Elda.

21:11.380 --> 21:14.290
This is as far as I can go, so good luck, El...

21:18.960 --> 21:20.790
Huh? Huh?!

21:21.750 --> 21:25.830
Hey... w-wait, Elda! Miko can't enter the sanctuary...

21:25.830 --> 21:27.080
It's fine.

21:28.170 --> 21:30.250
Just stay with me a bit longer.

21:33.460 --> 21:38.080
I-I'm scared of going alone.
If I fall, we fall together, okay?

21:38.080 --> 21:39.630
I'm telling you, you're not gonna fall!

21:52.790 --> 21:56.080
I pray that Elda never makes that face again.

22:03.080 --> 22:06.960
I was finally able to introduce you to Ieyasu-kun.

22:11.580 --> 22:14.420
I pray Elda is in good health forever!

22:15.080 --> 22:18.920
I-I pray that Koito has fun every day.

22:22.790 --> 22:28.250
I pray that even if I buy the slightly expensive toy
that comes out next month, Koito won't be angry with me.

22:30.710 --> 22:35.540
I pray that Elda will stop wasting her offerings
and gaming through the night!

22:38.250 --> 22:42.080
I-I pray that Koito will be kinder to me!

22:42.080 --> 22:45.130
I pray that Elda will become more serious
about performing her rituals!

22:45.130 --> 22:48.580
I pray that Koito will stop telling me to go outside!

22:48.580 --> 22:51.250
I pray Elda will stop being a shut-in!

22:53.170 --> 22:56.130
Morning has come once again in Tokyo.
